[Music]  slender man or that lanky faceless  tentacle wielding child stealing  teleporting creeps that's been haunting  our dreams for the last few years has  been traipsing across various electronic  mediums from its humble form beginnings  the figure has spawned endless fan art  from online artist communities fan  videos mockumentary  films and range of videogames Slender  Man is evolved into many different forms  through various threads turning him into  a community created terror that refuses  to leave us alone but what is it about  him that keeps us so intrigued  slenderman's creation began in something  Awful's forums in June of 2009 by user  victor serge two old photos of random  kids contained a tall dark creepy guy in  the background purposely vague to allow  for audience interpretation he has  typically portrayed as a tall thin  figure with a featureless head and a  black suit the photographs inspired  hundreds of stories found on forum  threads adding to the myth and horror of  Slender Man early stories depicted him  as dangerous and physically violent over  time though a second version of Slender  Man appeared one who was more passive  aggressive inflicting damage mentally  slowly forcing a victim to fall into  madness a few short weeks after the  character debuted a video series called  Marble Hornets appeared on YouTube  showing a behind-the-scenes of a film  project that slowly unravels into a  series revolving around Slenderman over  time thousands of Slender Man stories  emerged most of which seemed to focus on  the protagonist being haunted by the  tall cloaked shadowy figure three years  after those fateful forum posts youtuber  agent parsec created slender the eight  pages a simple unity based horror game  that places you on the terrifying turf  of the mysterious killer the dark woods  armed with nothing but a flashlight the  user has to find eight pages randomly  placed throughout the area each note you  get shortens your site and Slenderman  becomes increasingly aggressive video  and audio distortions add to the feeling  that he is somewhere near you all the  time and you get an incredible feeling  of helplessness and fear from the  paranoia that he's watching you and  planning your eventual demise  the sequel to the eight pages slender  the arrival released in 2013  similarly to the first game you get  nothing but a flashlight and the ability  to run to avoid your imminent doom but  the arrival offered something new a bit  more story and context the story about a  woman named Lauren investigating the  disappearance of her friend story about  strange discoveries of other  disappearances and eventually about how  all the people who had interactions with  Slender Man had subsequently exhibited  erratic terrifying behavior and this is  where Slender Man gets really  interesting because what you start to  understand is Slender Man himself isn't  the main thing to fear it's what happens  to people once they encounter him how  frightened and crazed they become in  their obsession with him  what makes Slender Man such a terrifying  monster is what he can make you become  as a result of your experiences and  state of mind a mistake that some people  had taken so seriously it's had  real-world consequences when two girls  from Wisconsin stabbed a classmate 19  times and claimed it was an offering for  Slender Man  now obviously Slender Man doesn't make  people kill and creepypasta doesn't make  people kill Slender Man is just a  fictitious character and this is an  anomaly so why are people so interested  thunderman is so popular in mainstream  media not because he's the ideal villain  for the internet because he was created  by the Internet within a few quick years  a simple forum post have so much  backstory that the world was able to  mould Slenderman into whatever they  feared the most  think about Bloody Mary or a monster  under the bed what's so frightening is  the unknown so we fill the gaps with  whatever scares us the most Slenderman  is ambiguous on purpose  so that we decide what's so terrifying  about him new Slender Man stories are  constantly being  and with the recent port of the arrival  to current gen platforms and a likely  sequel on the way  seems like Slenderman will be constantly  supplying us with a way to get scared  Slenderman doesn't look like he'll be  going away anytime soon and you get to  decide what's so frightening about that

